Scott's Theorem 7.2 defines the approximable application map from the product of the function space B → C with B into C. It relates a product token set s to an output set t when s is product-consistent, t is consistent, and the function space entails the first component of s by the function token whose input is the second component of s and whose output is t. The empty relation, closure under output union, and monotonicity are proved from the entailment laws of the function space and of C.
